# Release-parity baseline — holes that exist and are ACCEPTED, with the reason.
#
# Read by .github/scripts/check_release_parity.py. One `version  # reason` per
# line. Anything NOT listed here that has no GitHub Release is a hard CI failure.
#
# WHY A BASELINE AT ALL. This gate would otherwise ship red: 7 of the 16 versions
# this repo has claimed to ship have no Release. A gate that cannot go green gets
# muted inside a week, and a muted gate is worse than no gate — it looks like
# coverage. So the existing holes are recorded here, once, and the gate then
# fails only on NEW divergence.
#
# EVERY REASON BELOW IS VERIFIED, NOT PLAUSIBLE. A confident wrong note is what
# the next person trusts instead of re-checking, which is why the repo this gate
# came from records three of its own holes as "cause unestablished" rather than
# guessing. This repo needs no such category — see below.
#
# THE MEASUREMENT, 2026-08-12, against origin/main @ a989d28:
#
#   309d720  2026-05-29  "ci: add structure validation + release-on-version-bump
#                         automation (#10)"
#            introduced BOTH `VERSION` (at 1.7.0) and `.github/workflows/release.yml`,
#            in that one commit. Confirmed with --diff-filter=A on each path:
#              git log --diff-filter=A -- VERSION                        -> 309d720
#              git log --diff-filter=A -- .github/workflows/release.yml  -> 309d720
#              git show 309d720:VERSION                                  -> 1.7.0
#
#   Every value VERSION has held since, and its release:
#     1.7.0 (309d720, 2026-05-29) -> v1.7.0       1.10.2 (f3b06e21) -> v1.10.2
#     1.8.0 (74822de8, 2026-06-01) -> v1.8.0      1.10.3 (1efc65a5) -> v1.10.3
#     1.9.0 (a06ab8a3, 2026-06-05) -> v1.9.0      1.10.4 (cd79d78c) -> v1.10.4
#     1.10.0 (5c70b4e0, 2026-07-03) -> v1.10.0    1.11.0 (a989d28d) -> v1.11.0
#     1.10.1 (ebb228a8, 2026-08-05) -> v1.10.1
#   Nine values, nine releases, no gaps. Git tags likewise start at v1.7.0, so
#   there are no orphan tags-without-releases either.
#
# THE VERDICT THIS RECORDS. `release.yml` here carried the same
# `paths: ['VERSION']` filter that lost v1.13.0 upstream, right up until the
# commit that adds this file. It cost this repo NOTHING. Bug present, damage
# none — and that was measured rather than assumed, because a guard telling you
# a state is wrong does not tell you what the wrong state already cost.

# --- pre-date both VERSION and the release automation ---
